    narr:narration """The review opens with [an outside assessment request before a board submission](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_1) and [an agreement to evaluate the plan directly](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_2). The discussion details [a sequential four-site migration approach with soak windows](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_3), which meets [strong advisory endorsement over big-bang precedents](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_4) alongside [evidence from prior programme reversals](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_5). The advisor warns of [predictable schedule compression pressures](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_7) and issues [a directive to document rationale early](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_9). The critique then shifts to [the absence of an independent data-quality gate](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_13), separating [source data quality from migration movement validation](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_15) and specifying [independent gate ownership outside the project lead](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_17). The feedback concludes with [guidance to budget for gate-induced schedule delays](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_21), [affirmation of reference data and archiving strategy](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_25), and [agreement to present the quality gap openly to the board](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_28).""" ;
